# Line endings: LF in the repository, LF in the working tree on every platform.
#
# This snapshot was committed from a Windows checkout, so CRLF ended up in the
# index and `./gradlew` stopped executing on Linux CI (`cannot execute: required
# file not found` — the shebang gets a trailing CR). Normalizing keeps the tree
# identical on Windows, Linux, macOS and CI.
* text=auto

# Entry points must stay LF or they do not run on Linux/macOS.
gradlew text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf

# Windows batch files want CRLF.
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Binaries: never rewrite these.
*.jar binary
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.keystore binary
*.so binary
